  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U6", "U3", "U5", "U8"],
      "pins": ["U10.8", "U6.8", "U3.8", "U5.8", "U8.8"],
      "nets": ["NET0003"],
      "observed": "On the I2C-sensors sheet the PDIS pin (8) of both ADM3260 isolators (U10 for pH, U6 for EC) is labelled NET0003, and on the peristaltic-pump sheet the PD/UART pin (8) of all three TMC2209 drivers (U3, U5, U8) is also labelled NET0003; the SoC connects NET0003 to its single-wire UART pin group through R34 (1k). Thus the EZO isolator power-disable line and the stepper single-wire UART bus (STEP_BUS) are merged onto one net.",
      "expected": "The specification treats these as two separate signals: the EZO_PDIS net ties U3/U4 pin 8 to ESP32 IO6/SPI_CLK, while the shared TMC2209 UART (STEP_BUS) is on IO21/IO22. They must remain distinct nets so firmware can power-cycle the pH/EC isolators independently of the stepper bus.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "An EZO_PDIS net ties both U3 pin 8 and U4 pin 8 (PDIS) to a single ESP32 pin (IO6/SPI_CLK) [§4.2]"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "STEP_BUS (shared UART) | IO21/IO22 [§4.4 cross-check table]"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U10 pin 8 PDIS and U6 pin 8 PDIS carry label NET0003; U3/U5/U8 pin 8 PD/UART carry label NET0003 (sheets 1 and 2)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The pH/EC isolator power-disable pin is shorted to the stepper UART bus. Any activity on the UART line (or its idle pull-up via R34) will enable/disable the galvanically isolated I2C bridges to the EZO-pH and EZO-EC circuits, and the PDIS pins load the UART bus. Firmware can no longer power-cycle the probes independently of the dosing drivers, corrupting I2C sensor reads and stepper communication.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic merges the EZO isolator PDIS line (U10.8, U6.8) with the TMC2209 single-wire UART bus (U3/U5/U8.8) on net NET0003, whereas the specification requires EZO_PDIS (IO6) and STEP_BUS (IO21/IO22) to be separate nets; this net bridge is the only deviation the drawing supports."
}

